{"id":17338,"name":"Kent County","slug":"kent-county","state":"Maryland","code":"MD","program":null,"sourceUrl":"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/tax-lien/tax-lien-states/maryland-tax-liens-earn-solid-as-a-beginner/kent-county/","lastUpdated":"2026-07-13T12:29:54","facts":{"taxSaleType":"Tax Lien Certificates","redemptionPeriod":"6 months to 2 years","interestRate":"10% annually","bidProcedure":"Sealed bid system","deposit":"Required at the time of purchase","extra":[{"label":"Typical Date of Sale","value":"2nd Thursday in May"}]},"bodyHtml":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<span class=\"GDjqRhGHm24FsykZbJPpclVQbfFxmi7u0qWsCd1Jd8TMlw2tOvfNB17I9QYZnBEKeXrupAR3CrIPtLzoh\"><iframe title=\"Secret to Solid 10% Annual Returns - Kent County - Maryland Tax Lien Investing\" width=\"1170\" height=\"658\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/jXJc9roGkWI?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe></span>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-16018d1d wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://linktr.ee/dustinhahnrealestateinvesting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Click Here to Get Dustin Hahn’s Tax Lien and Deed FREE Mini-Course</a></div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Unlock-High-Returns-at-Kent-County,-Maryland's-Tax-Lien-Sale\">Unlock High Returns at Kent County, Maryland&#8217;s Tax Lien Sale</h1>\n\n\n\n<p>Kent County, Maryland, offers a lucrative opportunity for tax lien investors, with an annual tax lien sale providing a steady 10% return. This article guides you through the essential details of participating in the tax lien sales in Kent County.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Engage in Kent County&#8217;s tax lien sale to potentially secure high returns. With a 10% annual interest rate, this investment avenue is attractive for those looking to diversify their portfolio. The entry costs are relatively low compared to traditional property acquisitions, making it an accessible investment opportunity.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Understanding-Tax-Lien-Certificates\">Understanding Tax Lien Certificates</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Tax lien certificates represent a lien placed on a property due to unpaid taxes. Investors purchase these certificates at auction, earning interest until the property owner redeems the lien. If the owner fails to redeem within the specified period, the investor can initiate foreclosure proceedings to gain ownership.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Example-Investment\">Example Investment</h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Initial Purchase</strong>: $1,000 tax lien certificate.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Interest Earned</strong>: 10% annually, equating to $100 per year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Potential Returns</strong>: $100 in one year, $200 in two years, etc., until redemption or foreclosure.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Steps to Start Tax Lien Investing in Kent County</h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>1. Research and Understand Local Laws</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Familiarize yourself with Maryland&#8217;s tax lien laws, especially those specific to Kent County. Understanding the legal framework is crucial for successful investing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>2. Visit the Local Treasurer&#8217;s Website</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://kent.marylandtaxsale.com/index.cfm?folder=showDocument&amp;documentName=taxCertificateProcess\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Kent County Tax Sale Information</mark></a></li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.kentcounty.com/finance\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Kent County Finance Department</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>3. Check the Auction Site</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Auction Site</strong>: <a href=\"https://kent.marylandtaxsale.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">Kent County Auction Site</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>4. Read Details About Tax Liens</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Understand the sale schedule, parcel inquiry process, and other essential details to make informed bids.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>5. Contact the County Office</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>For additional inquiries, contact the Kent County Department of Finance:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Phone</strong>: 410-778-7478</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:financeinfo@kentgov.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><mark style=\"background-color:rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)\" class=\"has-inline-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-color\">financeinfo@kentgov.org</mark></a></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Important-Details\">Important Details</h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"></figure>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><picture><source srcset=\"https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Kent-County-Courthouse-Maryland.webp 1081w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Kent-County-Courthouse-Maryland-541x360.webp 541w,https://vault.taxlienschool.com